1
00:00:01,152 --> 00:00:03,050
(Love In Sync)

2
00:00:10,128 --> 00:00:12,433
(Kim Myung Soo)

3
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:18,862
(Kang Min Ah)

4
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:41,986
(Love In Sync)

5
00:00:44,051 --> 00:00:45,051
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds...)

6
00:00:45,052 --> 00:00:46,080
(in this drama are fictitious and unrelated to reality.)

7
00:00:46,081 --> 00:00:47,151
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:00:55,561 --> 00:00:56,991
This is the highlight of the awards show.

9
00:00:57,061 --> 00:00:59,231
Soon, the actresses will vie for the spotlight...

10
00:00:59,301 --> 00:01:03,231
in a fierce battle of the gowns, right here on the red carpet.

11
00:01:03,331 --> 00:01:04,331
(32nd Korea Film Award)

12
00:01:04,401 --> 00:01:07,341
In this bloody battle, dubbed the "War of Flowers,"

13
00:01:07,871 --> 00:01:10,671
who will emerge as tonight's victor?

14
00:01:32,931 --> 00:01:34,431
Darn it. A pound.

15
00:01:34,931 --> 00:01:36,471
This darn pound.

16
00:01:37,501 --> 00:01:39,541
I told you I was only having three pieces of kimbap yesterday.

17
00:01:40,001 --> 00:01:41,801
So why'd you make me eat five? Why?

18
00:01:41,971 --> 00:01:43,871
Because I was worried you'd collapse.

19
00:01:45,681 --> 00:01:48,311
- A pound isn't even noticeable. - I can notice.

20
00:01:48,411 --> 00:01:49,411
Right.

21
00:01:51,251 --> 00:01:53,521
She's so intense.

22
00:01:58,591 --> 00:01:59,891
How many shots are we doing today?

23
00:01:59,961 --> 00:02:03,031
FYI, Han Yi Jin got 300, and Oh Soo Ah got 400.

24
00:02:03,431 --> 00:02:04,891
Then obviously...

25
00:02:04,961 --> 00:02:07,861
It'll be more, right? All right, let's do 600 then.

26
00:02:24,981 --> 00:02:26,221
Add more contour.

27
00:02:26,721 --> 00:02:27,851
Make it really alluring.

28
00:02:32,761 --> 00:02:34,661
Wow.

29
00:02:35,631 --> 00:02:37,131
Bravo.

30
00:02:42,231 --> 00:02:44,601
Stunning, as always.

31
00:02:47,101 --> 00:02:49,641
From any and every angle.

32
00:02:51,211 --> 00:02:53,741
I am flawlessly beautiful.

33
00:02:55,211 --> 00:02:56,351
You guys are so lucky.

34
00:02:56,811 --> 00:02:58,151
- Yes? - Lucky how?

35
00:02:58,211 --> 00:03:00,321
You get to gaze upon my beauty at every moment.

36
00:03:01,051 --> 00:03:02,421
Why go to the Louvre?

37
00:03:03,121 --> 00:03:04,191
Venus is standing right here.

38
00:03:04,751 --> 00:03:06,260
- Am I wrong? - You're right.

39
00:03:06,261 --> 00:03:07,561
- It's so true. - Absolutely.

40
00:03:07,621 --> 00:03:08,621
It's so, so true.

41
00:03:11,091 --> 00:03:12,231
It makes me so sad.

42
00:03:13,031 --> 00:03:15,501
Why can I only see myself in a mirror?

43
00:03:17,601 --> 00:03:19,201
It's so unfair. It's killing me.

44
00:03:20,701 --> 00:03:21,701
We're going to be late.

45
00:03:22,311 --> 00:03:25,911
- We should go. - I suppose. Let's go get my award.

46
00:03:30,981 --> 00:03:31,981
Why?

47
00:03:32,351 --> 00:03:34,221
You should've just beaten him half to death.

48
00:03:34,951 --> 00:03:38,091
- What? - He made your life a living hell.

49
00:03:38,721 --> 00:03:40,291
You have to pay him back for what he did.

50
00:03:41,391 --> 00:03:42,391
What are you talking about...

51
00:03:42,791 --> 00:03:44,431
What, are you afraid you'll lose?

52
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:47,631
- Are you chickening out? - No, I'm not.

53
00:03:48,001 --> 00:03:49,001
Then what is it?

54
00:03:49,471 --> 00:03:52,601
Now that it's time for revenge, do you feel sorry for that bastard?

55
00:03:52,801 --> 00:03:56,871
- Crazy? Do you know what he did? - My point exactly.

56
00:03:58,241 --> 00:04:00,981
That bastard is the reason you're in this pathetic state.

57
00:04:02,611 --> 00:04:04,611
You dropped out of school like you were running for your life...

58
00:04:05,151 --> 00:04:08,421
and now you're cooped up in your room, living every day in hell.

59
00:04:10,321 --> 00:04:13,791
You have to make that bastard feel this shitty too.

60
00:04:17,161 --> 00:04:18,331
An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth.

61
00:04:19,601 --> 00:04:20,601
Get it?

62
00:04:21,401 --> 00:04:24,231
Are you really sure this is okay?

63
00:04:25,401 --> 00:04:28,501
I'm relieved he seems more energetic than before, but...

64
00:04:29,211 --> 00:04:32,111
what if this leads to him doing something truly dangerous?

65
00:04:32,541 --> 00:04:34,241
Our first priority is to save his life.

66
00:04:36,581 --> 00:04:39,281
Seon Woo is suffering from depression, lethargy,

67
00:04:39,751 --> 00:04:41,821
and suicidal thoughts due to relentless bullying.

68
00:04:42,221 --> 00:04:45,591
What's the most effective way to restore his will to live?

69
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:49,161
Understanding and forgiving his abusers?

70
00:04:49,431 --> 00:04:51,831
Or distorting and forgetting what happened?

71
00:04:55,901 --> 00:04:56,901
Revenge.

72
00:04:58,371 --> 00:04:59,971
For people who want to give up everything...

73
00:05:00,041 --> 00:05:01,541
with full despair and rage,

74
00:05:02,771 --> 00:05:03,871
a thirst for revenge can be...

75
00:05:03,941 --> 00:05:05,641
a surprisingly powerful motivator to live.

76
00:05:09,951 --> 00:05:12,351
Sir, I know exactly what you're worried about.

77
00:05:13,081 --> 00:05:14,081
But...

78
00:05:15,551 --> 00:05:17,621
you're aware of my skills and experience...

79
00:05:18,421 --> 00:05:19,421
as a counselor.

80
00:05:20,591 --> 00:05:23,531
I promise I'll bring back the son you remember...

81
00:05:28,131 --> 00:05:30,031
as quickly as possible.

82
00:05:33,101 --> 00:05:36,111
Of course, you know what you're doing. I was worrying for nothing...

83
00:05:36,771 --> 00:05:38,141
Since you're here, why don't you stay for a meal?

84
00:05:38,411 --> 00:05:40,511
Our housekeeper is an excellent cook.

85
00:05:41,641 --> 00:05:42,951
Thank you for the offer, but...

86
00:05:44,351 --> 00:05:45,981
I have another appointment.

87
00:05:51,251 --> 00:05:52,251
I'm sorry.

88
00:05:53,091 --> 00:05:54,091
Yes, this is Cha Eun Hwan.

89
00:05:55,591 --> 00:05:56,591
Yes.

90
00:05:57,791 --> 00:05:58,931
Yes. Where did you say you were from?

91
00:05:59,431 --> 00:06:02,031
You know our show, right? "Luckies on the Block."

92
00:06:02,431 --> 00:06:04,771
It's a pretty famous show. All you have to do is make an appearance...

93
00:06:04,831 --> 00:06:06,901
and your public recognition will skyrocket overnight.

94
00:06:08,771 --> 00:06:09,941
Yes, I'm well aware,

95
00:06:10,341 --> 00:06:12,141
but I have more than enough recognition as it is.

96
00:06:13,511 --> 00:06:16,851
But it's TV. It's on a whole new level compared to word of mouth.

97
00:06:17,381 --> 00:06:19,681
Well, I'm not really...

98
00:06:23,251 --> 00:06:24,251
Hello?

99
00:06:25,091 --> 00:06:28,421
- Excuse me. Excuse me, Counselor. - Oh, yes.

100
00:06:29,361 --> 00:06:30,561
I appreciate the offer,

101
00:06:31,761 --> 00:06:34,461
but I'm afraid I'll have to pass.

102
00:06:43,771 --> 00:06:45,511
("From Colleagues To Rivals, Han Yi Jin Versus Yu Ji An.")

103
00:06:45,571 --> 00:06:47,941
("Who Will Be Awarded In The Best New Artist Award Tonight?")

104
00:06:52,581 --> 00:06:53,851
Your jaw is going to fall off.

105
00:06:54,381 --> 00:06:55,751
How many pieces of gum are you chewing?

106
00:06:56,321 --> 00:06:58,051
What other choice do I have to reduce the puffiness?

107
00:06:58,651 --> 00:06:59,791
You think just anyone can become a star?

108
00:07:00,521 --> 00:07:01,991
This is all part of self-maintenance.

109
00:07:02,321 --> 00:07:04,061
Don't you know what being a professional is?

110
00:07:05,391 --> 00:07:06,931
Hey.

111
00:07:08,801 --> 00:07:10,801
What is it? You keep sneaking glances at me...

112
00:07:10,871 --> 00:07:12,471
like a puppy that needs to go out.

113
00:07:12,741 --> 00:07:15,541
- What is it? - Well, before we leave,

114
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:18,171
the CEO called.

115
00:07:18,611 --> 00:07:19,611
CEO Kim? What about him?

116
00:07:20,911 --> 00:07:23,411
Well, I'm not sure how I should tell you this...

117
00:07:23,481 --> 00:07:24,611
What is it?

118
00:07:26,251 --> 00:07:29,251
Hey, before I tell you, can we agree on three things?

119
00:07:30,421 --> 00:07:32,321
First, no getting mad.

120
00:07:32,821 --> 00:07:36,591
Second, no yelling. And third, no cursing.

121
00:07:36,991 --> 00:07:39,761
If you can promise me that, then I'll tell you.

122
00:07:42,831 --> 00:07:44,601
I promise, okay?

123
00:07:48,101 --> 00:07:49,101
So, you know...

124
00:07:53,081 --> 00:07:55,381
What kind of bullshit is that?

125
00:07:57,981 --> 00:08:00,651
(Yu Star)

126
00:08:01,551 --> 00:08:02,651
Just answer the call.

127
00:08:02,991 --> 00:08:05,591
What? Answer it so I can get chewed out?

128
00:08:05,921 --> 00:08:08,261
It's better than getting cussed out to your face.

129
00:08:08,521 --> 00:08:10,731
Getting yelled at over the phone is better, right?

130
00:08:10,791 --> 00:08:12,631
You have an image to maintain as the CEO.

131
00:08:15,061 --> 00:08:16,801
Darn, that's strangely persuasive.

132
00:08:17,331 --> 00:08:19,541
(J.An Entertainment)

133
00:08:21,841 --> 00:08:25,111
- Hey, Yu Star. What's up? - Why is the order so messed up?

134
00:08:25,441 --> 00:08:27,481
Why am I scheduled before Han Yi Jin? Why?

135
00:08:28,711 --> 00:08:30,111
Ji An.

136
00:08:30,711 --> 00:08:33,381
Calm down and listen to me, okay?

137
00:08:34,021 --> 00:08:37,251
The organizers set the schedule and just notified us.

138
00:08:37,321 --> 00:08:38,921
What was I supposed to do?

139
00:08:39,261 --> 00:08:41,021
So they told you to jump, and you asked how high?

140
00:08:41,091 --> 00:08:43,961
Like some stray dog rolling over and showing its belly? Just like that?

141
00:08:44,161 --> 00:08:46,101
Hey, does your mouth have to be so foul?

142
00:08:46,601 --> 00:08:48,031
Do you think this is like changing the lineup...

143
00:08:48,101 --> 00:08:49,101
for a girl group's music show?

144
00:08:49,571 --> 00:08:52,171
This is a prestigious film festival in the country.

145
00:08:52,231 --> 00:08:53,301
When they decide something,

146
00:08:53,371 --> 00:08:55,771
how can the CEO of a small agency change it?

147
00:08:56,111 --> 00:08:58,011
If I make a fuss trying to change it,

148
00:08:58,071 --> 00:09:00,411
I'll get on the industry's bad side, you know?

149
00:09:00,481 --> 00:09:01,641
Besides, people already say you're a...

150
00:09:03,511 --> 00:09:07,551
There are already rampant rumors about you being rude,

151
00:09:07,721 --> 00:09:09,521
so we don't need to add fuel to the fire.

152
00:09:09,851 --> 00:09:12,491
- I'm just thinking of you. - CEO.

153
00:09:13,591 --> 00:09:15,361
Can't you hear that sound?

154
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:17,791
Why? What sound?

155
00:09:18,231 --> 00:09:20,031
The sound of my reputation taking a nosedive.

156
00:09:20,931 --> 00:09:23,231
Don't you know what placement and order mean in this business?

157
00:09:23,671 --> 00:09:27,271
Putting me before Han Yi Jin means that she's ranked higher than me.

158
00:09:27,471 --> 00:09:30,941
And you want me to just accept that in front of everyone?

159
00:09:31,011 --> 00:09:32,011
Are you insane?

160
00:09:32,341 --> 00:09:34,741
Even as an idol, I was always in the center position.

161
00:09:34,941 --> 00:09:37,711
Hey, so what? Things have changed now.

162
00:09:40,421 --> 00:09:42,791
What has changed?

163
00:09:43,091 --> 00:09:44,691
(Kim Jun Sik)

164
00:09:47,721 --> 00:09:48,891
What I mean is...

165
00:09:50,561 --> 00:09:52,061
that it's already been decided.

166
00:09:52,491 --> 00:09:55,561
- Turn a blind eye this one time... - And?

167
00:09:55,831 --> 00:09:58,701
You can't fix it. Is that it?

168
00:09:59,301 --> 00:10:01,101
It's not that I can't...

169
00:10:01,401 --> 00:10:03,311
I'm trying to say it's beyond my capabilities.

170
00:10:05,411 --> 00:10:06,411
Fine.

171
00:10:06,741 --> 00:10:09,751
- If you can't, then I will. - Do what?

172
00:10:10,251 --> 00:10:11,981
Hey, hey, Ji An. Hey, Yu Star.

173
00:10:12,251 --> 00:10:16,591
Don't do it, okay? Don't do anything, you hear? Hey, Ji An.

174
00:10:19,791 --> 00:10:22,021
What kind of crazy stunt is she about to pull?

175
00:10:31,871 --> 00:10:32,871
Ram into them.

176
00:10:33,901 --> 00:10:36,311
- What? - I said, ram into them.

177
00:10:36,711 --> 00:10:38,971
Ma'am, you're not serious, are you?

178
00:10:40,541 --> 00:10:41,541
Right, you are serious.

179
00:10:50,821 --> 00:10:52,991
Your performance in your latest film was wonderful.

180
00:10:53,661 --> 00:10:56,091
I just love how vibrant your acting is.

181
00:10:56,691 --> 00:10:58,931
It really feels like the character is alive.

182
00:11:00,461 --> 00:11:02,871
That's only because I learned by watching you, ma'am.

183
00:11:04,071 --> 00:11:05,631
Listen to how sweet you are.

184
00:11:09,371 --> 00:11:10,371
Han Yi Jin.

185
00:11:11,111 --> 00:11:12,171
I'm sorry, but we're going to have...

186
00:11:12,241 --> 00:11:13,581
to ask you to switch places in the lineup.

187
00:11:17,381 --> 00:11:18,481
No one was badly injured,

188
00:11:18,911 --> 00:11:20,551
but they just have to make a quick stop at the hospital.

189
00:11:21,021 --> 00:11:22,181
We apologize and ask for your understanding.

190
00:11:30,761 --> 00:11:31,931
My today is our...

191
00:11:31,991 --> 00:11:33,001
You're so beautiful.

192
00:11:33,931 --> 00:11:36,031
- Please look this way. - That was Han Yi Jin...

193
00:11:36,101 --> 00:11:37,601
who is cementing her place as a true actress.

194
00:11:38,131 --> 00:11:39,971
Her outstanding acting also earned her a nomination...

195
00:11:40,041 --> 00:11:41,141
for the Best New Artist Award.

196
00:11:51,051 --> 00:11:52,051
Wow.

197
00:11:54,721 --> 00:11:58,191
And Yu Ji An has finally made her grand entrance on the red carpet.

198
00:11:58,721 --> 00:12:00,621
As always, she is absolutely stunning.

199
00:12:01,291 --> 00:12:03,531
We heard she was in a car accident on the way here,

200
00:12:03,591 --> 00:12:04,761
so we hope she's all right.

201
00:12:12,171 --> 00:12:14,471
- Look over here, please. - Over here.

202
00:12:15,801 --> 00:12:17,871
What is she doing? Why is she just standing there and not moving?

203
00:12:18,511 --> 00:12:20,111
I'll go when you go.

204
00:12:24,781 --> 00:12:28,881
Wow. It looks as though they're planning on walking in together.

205
00:12:35,121 --> 00:12:37,791
Their friendship, which has lasted since their days in a girl group...

206
00:12:38,031 --> 00:12:40,661
is truly making for a beautiful night.

207
00:12:41,101 --> 00:12:43,701
What's this? An unwelcome reception?

208
00:12:44,171 --> 00:12:45,631
I didn't think we were that close.

209
00:12:46,271 --> 00:12:48,371
Just think of it as a little show for the public.

210
00:12:49,001 --> 00:12:50,271
You're good at that, aren't you?

211
00:13:02,021 --> 00:13:03,121
Please look over here.

212
00:13:03,321 --> 00:13:05,151
Ji An, could you look to the right, please?

213
00:13:05,221 --> 00:13:08,321
- Please look this way too. - Could you two give us a smile?

214
00:13:16,831 --> 00:13:20,101
They're both nominated for the Best New Actress Award tonight.

215
00:13:20,501 --> 00:13:23,141
Their friendship is strong, so whoever wins...

216
00:13:23,341 --> 00:13:26,411
I'm sure they'll both be sincerely cheering for each other.

217
00:13:27,141 --> 00:13:29,981
The best of friends and friendly rivals.

218
00:13:30,051 --> 00:13:32,751
A relationship like that is truly enviable.

219
00:13:33,081 --> 00:13:36,821
And speaking of nominees, here comes another one now, Kwon Hyun Jin.

220
00:13:36,891 --> 00:13:38,591
- Gosh, it's freezing. - Welcome.

221
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:40,391
I'm hungry. Feed me. Food.

222
00:13:41,261 --> 00:13:44,291
Oh, gosh. Look what the cat dragged in.

223
00:13:44,861 --> 00:13:45,991
Feed me.

224
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:49,161
I'm so hungry. So hungry.

225
00:13:51,701 --> 00:13:52,730
So cold.

226
00:13:52,731 --> 00:13:56,710
Next, let's see the nomination of Music Awards.

227
00:13:56,711 --> 00:13:58,040
Let's check out the first nominee.

228
00:13:58,041 --> 00:14:01,311
Dude, you really ought to eat a proper meal every once in a while.

229
00:14:01,811 --> 00:14:03,081
I wish I could.

230
00:14:03,281 --> 00:14:05,981
But an hour of my time is far too valuable to waste on a single meal.

231
00:14:06,351 --> 00:14:10,791
- You know what I charge per hour. - Oh, I'm well aware...

232
00:14:11,221 --> 00:14:13,121
that you'd win a gold medal for being obnoxious.

233
00:14:13,661 --> 00:14:16,631
- Hey... - Be quiet. I'm watching this.

234
00:14:16,891 --> 00:14:18,691
You started it.

235
00:14:18,761 --> 00:14:21,201
Now, let's move on to our next nomination.

236
00:14:21,431 --> 00:14:24,031
Why is a guy who only watches porn watching an awards show?

237
00:14:24,371 --> 00:14:27,941
Hey, my favorite star is up for the Best New Artist Award.

238
00:14:28,171 --> 00:14:31,471
As a fan, I have to be part of this glorious moment.

239
00:14:32,511 --> 00:14:35,681
- What are you talking about? Who? - Who do you think? Yu Ji An?

240
00:14:36,451 --> 00:14:39,111
I was even the Fan Club President at one point.

241
00:14:40,581 --> 00:14:42,121
You've had tons of "shes" like that.

242
00:14:42,181 --> 00:14:44,191
If you think someone's even a little pretty,

243
00:14:44,591 --> 00:14:46,861
you're signing up for their fan clubs right away.

244
00:14:48,621 --> 00:14:51,931
Why do you always have to like...

245
00:14:52,561 --> 00:14:55,731
Hey, what's wrong with my Ji An?

246
00:14:57,301 --> 00:15:00,841
Oh, right. Because she's your crush's rival?

247
00:15:00,901 --> 00:15:02,801
What crush? No, it's not like that.

248
00:15:02,871 --> 00:15:06,781
- Hey, just go out with her already. - I said no.

249
00:15:07,581 --> 00:15:09,341
Do you want me to sue you for spreading false rumors?

250
00:15:09,651 --> 00:15:11,381
- It's really not true? - No.

251
00:15:12,581 --> 00:15:14,081
That's ridiculous...

252
00:15:14,921 --> 00:15:18,491
First, let's watch the nominations for the Best New Actress Award.

253
00:15:20,561 --> 00:15:22,520
You're lying, right? A car accident?

254
00:15:22,521 --> 00:15:24,830
The first nominee is...

255
00:15:24,831 --> 00:15:26,531
Is your suspicious nature incurable?

256
00:15:27,131 --> 00:15:29,130
How have you not been cured yet?

257
00:15:29,131 --> 00:15:30,530
Her role was a murderer...

258
00:15:30,531 --> 00:15:32,401
It's all thanks to your pathological lying.

259
00:15:33,501 --> 00:15:35,141
You were like this when you were an idol too.

260
00:15:35,571 --> 00:15:38,011
Whenever there was a gig you didn't want to do,

261
00:15:38,071 --> 00:15:40,141
you'd whine that you were sick or tired.

262
00:15:40,541 --> 00:15:41,611
And you'd just slip away.

263
00:15:42,381 --> 00:15:43,851
Thanks to you, the rest of us suffered.

264
00:15:44,381 --> 00:15:48,081
If you call that suffering, then I must have bled to death.

265
00:15:49,991 --> 00:15:52,791
While you guys had just 1 gig and 1 practice,

266
00:15:53,361 --> 00:15:54,920
I was sleeping four hours a day,

267
00:15:54,921 --> 00:15:56,491
running from variety shows to events.

268
00:15:57,391 --> 00:15:59,191
Thanks to that, our group got famous...

269
00:15:59,731 --> 00:16:02,301
and I even split the money I worked myself to death with you.

270
00:16:03,431 --> 00:16:06,401
That's why our fans called me the "charity angel,"

271
00:16:06,871 --> 00:16:08,501
and you guys were the "parasites."

272
00:16:09,501 --> 00:16:12,010
The next nominee is...

273
00:16:12,011 --> 00:16:13,140
Because of those hateful comments,

274
00:16:13,141 --> 00:16:15,810
Yu Ju was even hospitalized for depression.

275
00:16:15,811 --> 00:16:17,150
Because of a critical mistake...

276
00:16:17,151 --> 00:16:18,581
And as if that wasn't enough,

277
00:16:18,651 --> 00:16:20,751
you selfishly left and our group disbanded.

278
00:16:20,821 --> 00:16:22,381
That just means she was weak.

279
00:16:24,251 --> 00:16:26,491
- What? Weak? - It amplified...

280
00:16:26,961 --> 00:16:28,391
Let's get our facts straight.

281
00:16:29,561 --> 00:16:31,261
Why is the group's disbandment my fault?

282
00:16:31,691 --> 00:16:32,761
You're asking because you don't know?

283
00:16:33,931 --> 00:16:35,000
As soon as you got popular,

284
00:16:35,001 --> 00:16:37,831
- you ditched us and went solo. - That's why...

285
00:16:38,671 --> 00:16:41,471
A group that disbands just because one member leaves...

286
00:16:42,771 --> 00:16:44,971
Doesn't that just mean you guys were hopelessly incompetent?

287
00:16:46,481 --> 00:16:47,580
In the past...

288
00:16:47,581 --> 00:16:51,051
Why should I feel responsible or sorry for your incompetence?

289
00:16:51,881 --> 00:16:53,181
In this competitive world.

290
00:16:56,651 --> 00:16:58,590
- You're right. - It's really...

291
00:16:58,591 --> 00:17:00,960
- That's true. - Whoever gets the award...

292
00:17:00,961 --> 00:17:03,131
The fact that we were tossed aside as soon as you left...

293
00:17:04,291 --> 00:17:05,931
must be because we were incompetent.

294
00:17:07,501 --> 00:17:08,501
Okay, next up, we have the presentation...

295
00:17:08,561 --> 00:17:11,671
- of the Best New Actress Award. - But...

296
00:17:11,901 --> 00:17:14,001
- Presenting is last year's winner, - Aren't you curious?

297
00:17:14,241 --> 00:17:16,341
- Park Hyo Jin. - About what?

298
00:17:16,411 --> 00:17:17,411
Let's welcome her to the stage.

299
00:17:19,571 --> 00:17:21,381
(Korea Film Award, Best New Actress Award)

300
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,751
- Now that the tables have turned, - Hello.

301
00:17:26,551 --> 00:17:29,820
- who's the incompetent one? - I'm really grateful...

302
00:17:29,821 --> 00:17:31,390
When we were idols, you were the amazing center...

303
00:17:31,391 --> 00:17:33,321
and I was the pathetic nobody.

304
00:17:34,061 --> 00:17:36,691
- But now that we're actors? - I think...

305
00:17:37,161 --> 00:17:39,391
- Who's the center? - The 32nd Korea Film Awards.

306
00:17:39,461 --> 00:17:41,831
- And who's the nobody? - The Best New Actress Award is...

307
00:17:46,301 --> 00:17:48,471
going to Han Yi Jin for "I Was Wrong."

308
00:17:49,641 --> 00:17:50,741
Congratulations.

309
00:17:51,141 --> 00:17:54,480
Han Yi Jin played a role of Kim Seon Hwa,

310
00:17:54,481 --> 00:17:56,780
a vicious character in "I Was Wrong,"

311
00:17:56,781 --> 00:17:59,921
who betrays her loved ones.

312
00:18:00,121 --> 00:18:02,051
With a delicate performance...

313
00:18:02,121 --> 00:18:04,851
that captured Kim Seon Hwa's growth through her tears,

314
00:18:04,921 --> 00:18:07,721
she was praised for doubling the character's charm.

315
00:18:11,691 --> 00:18:14,601
Why Han Yi Jin and not me?

316
00:18:15,101 --> 00:18:16,131
I...

317
00:18:16,631 --> 00:18:20,071
I worked so hard.

318
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:26,811
I worked really, really hard.

319
00:18:51,101 --> 00:18:53,341
Today, rather than the "throwing a fit" concept,

320
00:18:53,601 --> 00:18:55,441
it seems she's going for the "frost in May" concept.

321
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:59,411
She's crying like a ghost from a folktale, full of deep resentment.

322
00:19:01,611 --> 00:19:03,711
I thought maybe if she won the award,

323
00:19:04,081 --> 00:19:06,111
I could use that chance while she's in a good mood...

324
00:19:06,181 --> 00:19:07,481
to slip her the contract renewal.

325
00:19:08,051 --> 00:19:11,321
But of course, Han Yi Jin had to be the one to win it.

326
00:19:11,821 --> 00:19:15,921
- Wow, you were dreaming big, boss. - What?

327
00:19:16,121 --> 00:19:19,291
Honestly, if she had won the Best New Artist Award today,

328
00:19:19,391 --> 00:19:22,601
that would have been proof that the organizers were corrupt.

329
00:19:23,061 --> 00:19:25,931
But based on tonight, it seems like a very fair awards ceremony.

330
00:19:26,201 --> 00:19:27,401
I have total faith in them now.

331
00:19:27,501 --> 00:19:29,871
As her manager, you should believe in and support...

332
00:19:29,941 --> 00:19:32,070
your star no matter what.

333
00:19:32,071 --> 00:19:35,041
I do. I totally support her.

334
00:19:35,141 --> 00:19:38,951
But fairness... Well, that's a whole different matter, you know?

335
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:44,851
But really, should we be hanging around here?

336
00:19:45,191 --> 00:19:48,861
Isn't it better to take off before we get caught in the fallout?

337
00:19:51,091 --> 00:19:52,861
"Isn't it better?" That's informal, kid.

338
00:19:54,101 --> 00:19:55,301
Don't you see it's raining out there?

339
00:19:56,161 --> 00:19:58,901
You know she goes nuts if we leave her alone when it's raining.

340
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:03,211
Hey.

341
00:20:03,841 --> 00:20:06,010
Let's wait for it to stop, then look for...

342
00:20:06,011 --> 00:20:08,081
- a chance to bolt. Got it? - Okay.

343
00:20:11,181 --> 00:20:13,081
Oh, you're out.

344
00:20:14,221 --> 00:20:15,551
Are you okay?

345
00:20:18,921 --> 00:20:20,121
I'm hungry.

346
00:20:41,911 --> 00:20:44,411
Here we go again.

347
00:21:08,901 --> 00:21:12,111
It's not much, but please enjoy.

348
00:21:13,011 --> 00:21:14,081
- This is a ton of food. - Okay.

349
00:21:14,911 --> 00:21:16,241
Are you really not going to eat?

350
00:21:16,881 --> 00:21:18,811
You should just eat to your heart's content on a day like this.

351
00:21:19,081 --> 00:21:20,421
Right, right, right.

352
00:21:20,481 --> 00:21:23,281
I already didn't win the award. You want me to get fat too?

353
00:21:27,461 --> 00:21:30,691
This is a feast for you two, so enjoy.

354
00:21:31,391 --> 00:21:33,801
Okay.

355
00:21:34,901 --> 00:21:38,331
Thanks. But seriously, how are we supposed to eat all this?

356
00:21:39,831 --> 00:21:42,871
- I'm getting in shape. - Shut it.

357
00:21:43,341 --> 00:21:44,711
Just listen while you eat.

358
00:21:46,241 --> 00:21:48,381
I'm just really curious about something.

359
00:21:49,011 --> 00:21:50,211
And I want you two to be honest.

360
00:21:51,451 --> 00:21:53,481
You have to tell me the absolute truth.

361
00:21:54,321 --> 00:21:55,321
- About what? - About what?

362
00:21:56,581 --> 00:21:57,791
My acting...

363
00:22:00,521 --> 00:22:02,021
Is it worse than Han Yi Jin's?

364
00:22:06,391 --> 00:22:08,801
I just can't wrap my head around it.

365
00:22:09,901 --> 00:22:11,471
The idea that I'm not as good as her?

366
00:22:13,801 --> 00:22:14,871
However...

367
00:22:16,441 --> 00:22:18,040
Crying in this situation is...

368
00:22:18,041 --> 00:22:19,971
- what amateurs do. - Exactly.

369
00:22:20,041 --> 00:22:22,041
So I'm going to analyze this like a professional.

370
00:22:22,381 --> 00:22:24,111
Today's judging results.

371
00:22:27,251 --> 00:22:30,021
Hey, what are you talking about? You're not worse than her.

372
00:22:30,391 --> 00:22:32,051
It's all just luck. Pure luck.

373
00:22:32,451 --> 00:22:35,891
- Awards are 80 percent luck anyway. - That's right.

374
00:22:41,331 --> 00:22:45,201
Look, honestly, everyone has a different reaction to acting.

375
00:22:45,401 --> 00:22:47,941
The whole idea of objectively judging something...

376
00:22:48,001 --> 00:22:49,301
so subjective is a joke.

377
00:22:49,801 --> 00:22:51,471
- Right? - Totally.

378
00:22:51,941 --> 00:22:54,241
From my perspective, your acting was way better.

379
00:22:56,681 --> 00:22:59,251
Oh, stop lying.

380
00:22:59,311 --> 00:23:00,421
- I'm serious. - I'm serious.

381
00:23:02,681 --> 00:23:06,051
No, don't be like that. I'm asking you to be completely honest.

382
00:23:06,251 --> 00:23:08,021
It's the only way I'll be able to improve.

383
00:23:08,321 --> 00:23:10,361
- It's true. - It's true.

384
00:23:11,391 --> 00:23:13,701
If you two keep lying, I'm going to get seriously angry.

385
00:23:13,901 --> 00:23:16,431
What? We're not lying.

386
00:23:17,331 --> 00:23:18,371
Seriously...

387
00:23:19,201 --> 00:23:20,541
Can I be honest?

388
00:23:24,341 --> 00:23:26,241
So you were lying this whole time.

389
00:23:29,711 --> 00:23:30,711
Go on.

390
00:23:31,011 --> 00:23:33,381
Tell me what you really, honestly think.

391
00:23:34,881 --> 00:23:35,951
Well...

392
00:23:36,721 --> 00:23:39,291
Out of a sense of duty as your manager,

393
00:23:39,351 --> 00:23:40,891
I analyzed your acting.

394
00:23:41,721 --> 00:23:43,931
It's not that you're a bad actor, but...

395
00:23:43,991 --> 00:23:46,031
how should I put this? It lacks soul.

396
00:23:48,301 --> 00:23:50,831
Soul?

397
00:23:51,171 --> 00:23:52,470
Like, you laugh when you're told to laugh...

398
00:23:52,471 --> 00:23:53,971
and cry when you're told to cry.

399
00:23:54,501 --> 00:23:58,871
I can't feel any understanding or immersion in the character.

400
00:24:00,811 --> 00:24:02,941
Is that what it looked like to you?

401
00:24:04,151 --> 00:24:08,351
- Look who's the critic. - No, I wouldn't go that far.

402
00:24:08,621 --> 00:24:10,951
But then I thought about why that might be.

403
00:24:11,091 --> 00:24:15,861
I think it might be because you lack empathy.

404
00:24:17,731 --> 00:24:21,001
Lack of empathy?

405
00:24:21,831 --> 00:24:24,971
Well, you don't really consider other people's perspectives.

406
00:24:25,131 --> 00:24:28,601
You tend to be a bit selfish and self-centered, don't you?

407
00:24:28,801 --> 00:24:30,371
And what is acting?

408
00:24:30,711 --> 00:24:34,581
It's about expressing another person's life and emotions.

409
00:24:34,911 --> 00:24:37,781
That's hard for someone like you. Don't you think?

410
00:24:49,091 --> 00:24:50,091
You can have the rest.

411
00:24:56,031 --> 00:24:57,031
Eat up.

412
00:25:05,011 --> 00:25:06,011
Oh, man.

413
00:25:06,941 --> 00:25:08,481
Hey, it's a good thing the rain stopped.

414
00:25:09,241 --> 00:25:10,511
If it hadn't, you and I...

415
00:25:10,581 --> 00:25:12,911
would have died a glorious death by food torture here today.

416
00:25:13,721 --> 00:25:15,080
- Sir. - Yes?

417
00:25:15,081 --> 00:25:16,581
Do you know a good place for antacids?

418
00:25:16,921 --> 00:25:18,321
- Antacids? - Yes.

419
00:25:18,551 --> 00:25:19,551
- Hey, Do Hoon. - Yes?

420
00:25:19,552 --> 00:25:21,321
Run, run, run.

421
00:25:21,791 --> 00:25:23,061
Running is best for indigestion, you fool. Run.

422
00:25:23,191 --> 00:25:25,161
- That won't work. - Run, run. Let's go.

423
00:25:26,191 --> 00:25:27,361
Why are you doing this to me?

424
00:25:28,301 --> 00:25:29,301
What are you talking about?

425
00:25:30,001 --> 00:25:31,571
What am I to you, Mom?

426
00:25:32,531 --> 00:25:33,531
Ye Rin.

427
00:25:33,941 --> 00:25:35,741
All you ever think about is my sister.

428
00:25:36,601 --> 00:25:38,671
What about me? I've spent my life worrying about you...

429
00:25:38,741 --> 00:25:39,771
because I felt sorry for you.

430
00:25:40,441 --> 00:25:41,511
Don't I get hurt too?

431
00:25:42,041 --> 00:25:43,751
- Am I made of steel? - And what is acting?

432
00:25:44,081 --> 00:25:47,981
It's about expressing another person's life and emotions.

433
00:25:48,221 --> 00:25:50,521
That's hard for someone like you.

434
00:25:55,661 --> 00:25:58,461
I'll try. Ready, action.

435
00:25:59,861 --> 00:26:00,901
Even Mom...

436
00:26:09,571 --> 00:26:11,211
The kids' juice that even moms want.

437
00:26:11,271 --> 00:26:13,641
A nutritious after-school snack, Juicy Juicy.

438
00:26:16,311 --> 00:26:18,281
The kids' juice that even moms want.

439
00:26:18,881 --> 00:26:21,651
A nutritious after-school snack, Juicy Juicy.

440
00:26:22,481 --> 00:26:24,891
Cut. That was excellent.

441
00:26:30,991 --> 00:26:31,991
Ji An.

442
00:26:33,361 --> 00:26:34,361
Why did you do that?

443
00:26:35,501 --> 00:26:39,031
What do you care if she forgets her lines?

444
00:26:40,031 --> 00:26:43,911
But they said you're supposed to help a friend in need.

445
00:26:44,341 --> 00:26:47,011
Who said that? What kind of idiot?

446
00:26:47,941 --> 00:26:51,351
Her mistake was your opportunity.

447
00:26:51,881 --> 00:26:55,081
Why? Why would you do something so stupid, why?

448
00:27:04,791 --> 00:27:05,791
Look at me.

449
00:27:07,431 --> 00:27:10,201
Do you want to go back to the orphanage?

450
00:27:17,041 --> 00:27:21,141
I don't want to live apart from you anymore, Ji An.

451
00:27:23,181 --> 00:27:24,181
For that to happen...

452
00:27:25,751 --> 00:27:27,281
You have to listen to me, right?

453
00:27:28,751 --> 00:27:29,751
Ji An.

454
00:27:30,491 --> 00:27:32,021
You must never...

455
00:27:34,091 --> 00:27:37,231
be the kind of person who needs to be nice to others.

456
00:27:38,761 --> 00:27:41,001
You need to be someone who doesn't have to be good.

457
00:27:43,261 --> 00:27:44,271
If you behave like that,

458
00:27:46,271 --> 00:27:49,471
the world will be nice to you...

459
00:27:51,541 --> 00:27:52,611
and treat you well.

460
00:27:54,111 --> 00:27:55,111
Understand?

461
00:28:12,591 --> 00:28:13,661
A gift.

462
00:28:17,171 --> 00:28:19,371
Thank you so much for earlier.

463
00:28:30,811 --> 00:28:33,711
Get lost. I'm telling you to get out of my sight.

464
00:28:35,281 --> 00:28:36,381
That's not it.

465
00:28:37,221 --> 00:28:38,351
That emotion right there...

466
00:28:38,991 --> 00:28:39,991
What about it?

467
00:28:40,591 --> 00:28:44,331
The stage directions say to shout in rage.

468
00:28:44,991 --> 00:28:46,861
But what kind of emotion do you think that is?

469
00:28:48,361 --> 00:28:50,261
She tells the man she loves to get lost,

470
00:28:50,401 --> 00:28:51,831
but deep down, she wants him to stay and hold her.

471
00:28:51,971 --> 00:28:54,501
That's the desperate feeling underneath it all.

472
00:28:55,001 --> 00:28:56,201
It's not just about screaming your head off.

473
00:28:59,371 --> 00:29:01,481
(Not Just Screaming)

474
00:29:02,881 --> 00:29:04,311
You don't understand what that feels like, do you?

475
00:29:06,981 --> 00:29:09,451
That's why your acting isn't improving.

476
00:29:13,351 --> 00:29:14,491
Let's take a short break.

477
00:29:22,301 --> 00:29:23,931
They're dissing you, right?

478
00:29:25,031 --> 00:29:27,031
I knew you were on the association's bad side, but to do it so openly...

479
00:29:27,901 --> 00:29:29,701
How can people be this petty? Seriously.

480
00:29:30,671 --> 00:29:34,381
The jealousy of lesser men is just something the great have to endure.

481
00:29:35,081 --> 00:29:36,711
Let them. It's actually kind of amusing.

482
00:29:38,351 --> 00:29:39,411
Today's the day for free consults, right?

483
00:29:39,881 --> 00:29:42,681
- Lee Young Ji's scheduled at 2pm. - Oh, yes.

484
00:29:43,181 --> 00:29:44,191
Sir.

485
00:29:45,521 --> 00:29:47,961
Should we send a bouquet to Yi Jin?

486
00:29:48,891 --> 00:29:51,891
She's a VIP at our clinic. We should at least congratulate her.

487
00:29:52,431 --> 00:29:54,131
Best New Artist Award.

488
00:30:03,371 --> 00:30:05,371
(Cha Eun Hwan)

489
00:30:11,381 --> 00:30:13,281
(Counselor Cha Eun Hwan)

490
00:30:16,581 --> 00:30:17,991
I enjoyed the awards ceremony yesterday.

491
00:30:18,451 --> 00:30:19,451
Congrats on the Best New Artist Award.

492
00:30:20,051 --> 00:30:21,061
Thank you.

493
00:30:21,391 --> 00:30:23,521
I wanted to hear you congratulate me more than anyone.

494
00:30:27,731 --> 00:30:28,861
I'll treat you to something big to celebrate.

495
00:30:29,331 --> 00:30:30,361
When are you free?

496
00:30:32,071 --> 00:30:34,341
You're here? One moment, please.

497
00:30:42,941 --> 00:30:45,211
What? You come here?

498
00:30:45,711 --> 00:30:46,711
I switched.

499
00:30:47,221 --> 00:30:49,551
The director kept begging me to come so she could show off her skills.

500
00:30:49,881 --> 00:30:50,891
You've really made it.

501
00:30:51,321 --> 00:30:53,351
The director here only works with the best of the best.

502
00:30:55,921 --> 00:30:56,921
Did you cry yesterday?

503
00:30:58,961 --> 00:31:00,831
Me? Why?

504
00:31:03,831 --> 00:31:05,531
Because you were upset that I won the award instead of you?

505
00:31:07,471 --> 00:31:08,601
I wasn't upset.

506
00:31:11,411 --> 00:31:13,811
My face is just puffy. I ate ramen.

507
00:31:15,711 --> 00:31:17,511
You? The girl who won't even swallow her own spit...

508
00:31:17,581 --> 00:31:19,011
after 6pm to avoid gaining weight?

509
00:31:22,051 --> 00:31:23,051
It was just one of those days.

510
00:31:23,651 --> 00:31:24,991
A day where you just want to let yourself go.

511
00:31:25,691 --> 00:31:26,691
Yesterday was that day.

512
00:31:27,321 --> 00:31:29,321
- So you were upset. - I said I wasn't.

513
00:31:31,961 --> 00:31:34,961
Ma'am, they said the car is waiting and to please come down.

514
00:31:36,501 --> 00:31:38,271
You're Mi Jeong, right?

515
00:31:40,841 --> 00:31:41,941
Hi, it's good to see you.

516
00:31:42,271 --> 00:31:43,401
Long time no see.

517
00:31:45,771 --> 00:31:46,941
You work for her?

518
00:31:48,111 --> 00:31:49,511
You must have your hands full.

519
00:31:55,581 --> 00:31:58,051
You should ask for some extra contouring today.

520
00:31:59,791 --> 00:32:00,791
Your face is as round as the moon.

521
00:32:02,261 --> 00:32:03,261
Unbelievable.

522
00:32:10,161 --> 00:32:13,201
Is my face really that puffy? Darn.

523
00:32:15,071 --> 00:32:17,971
Hey. I almost lost it watching the awards ceremony yesterday.

524
00:32:18,671 --> 00:32:19,671
About what?

525
00:32:19,741 --> 00:32:23,281
Whether it's class, looks, or popularity,

526
00:32:23,381 --> 00:32:26,181
how could Han Yi Jin win over you? Does that make any sense?

527
00:32:27,821 --> 00:32:30,751
I guess the judges thought differently.

528
00:32:31,351 --> 00:32:32,751
Look at how naive you are.

529
00:32:33,321 --> 00:32:34,391
There's a reason for everything, you know.

530
00:32:34,921 --> 00:32:37,331
A reason? What reason?

531
00:32:42,031 --> 00:32:44,901
Director Yoon, who was one of the judges, and Han Yi Jin...

532
00:32:45,571 --> 00:32:46,731
They have a thing going on.

533
00:32:48,401 --> 00:32:49,401
Hey.

534
00:32:50,601 --> 00:32:51,771
Do you know Yi Jin?

535
00:32:52,411 --> 00:32:53,411
Yes?

536
00:32:54,641 --> 00:32:56,111
I wouldn't say I know her...

537
00:32:56,581 --> 00:32:57,711
But I do know her.

538
00:32:58,551 --> 00:33:00,381
So shut up and do your job.

539
00:33:10,021 --> 00:33:11,191
Did you see Yu Ji An's outfit?

540
00:33:11,661 --> 00:33:13,331
She's wearing Erbeni. Why am I wearing Arden?

541
00:33:13,831 --> 00:33:17,061
Well... Erbeni doesn't sponsor just anyone.

542
00:33:17,331 --> 00:33:18,331
What makes me...

543
00:33:19,801 --> 00:33:20,801
just anyone?

544
00:33:21,571 --> 00:33:23,341
I don't care what it takes.

545
00:33:23,401 --> 00:33:26,371
Get Erbeni to sponsor me tomorrow. Got it?

546
00:33:27,011 --> 00:33:28,011
Yes.

547
00:33:29,511 --> 00:33:30,711
Yes, I'll be in touch.

548
00:33:32,751 --> 00:33:34,381
We just heard from Director Moon.

549
00:33:35,781 --> 00:33:36,781
Director Moon?

550
00:33:39,021 --> 00:33:40,021
The Moon Gyeong Sik?

551
00:33:40,351 --> 00:33:41,361
Yes.

552
00:33:41,591 --> 00:33:42,890
("Casting Moon Gyeong Sik's New Film")

553
00:33:42,891 --> 00:33:44,091
("Who Will Be Next Cinderella?")

554
00:33:50,931 --> 00:33:54,441
So, Director Moon is pushing for Han Yi Jin,

555
00:33:54,541 --> 00:33:56,271
but the production company is against it.

556
00:33:56,871 --> 00:33:58,141
She lacks star power, I guess.

557
00:33:58,641 --> 00:34:00,941
The production company is pushing for our Yu Ji An,

558
00:34:01,011 --> 00:34:02,441
but Director Moon is against it.

559
00:34:02,781 --> 00:34:04,081
She lacks acting skills, I guess.

560
00:34:05,981 --> 00:34:08,481
A showdown between star power and acting skills.

561
00:34:09,951 --> 00:34:12,151
But why isn't our Ji An's acting improving?

562
00:34:12,751 --> 00:34:14,321
If she stars in Director Moon's film,

563
00:34:14,391 --> 00:34:16,061
her acting career will be set for life.

564
00:34:18,431 --> 00:34:19,431
That's why, sir...

565
00:34:20,431 --> 00:34:22,931
I've come across some incredible information.

566
00:34:29,371 --> 00:34:30,641
(Cha Eun Hwan, Mental Counselor)

567
00:34:30,701 --> 00:34:33,871
So this guy's really that good?

568
00:34:34,581 --> 00:34:35,581
What is he, some Bodhisattva?

569
00:34:35,911 --> 00:34:39,081
No, he's a psychological counselor.

570
00:34:39,481 --> 00:34:42,021
They say he's amazing at reading people.

571
00:34:42,781 --> 00:34:44,791
He not only treats trauma and compulsions...

572
00:34:45,391 --> 00:34:48,961
but he also draws out emotions hidden in the subconscious.

573
00:34:49,061 --> 00:34:51,461
They say he even helps actors improve their skills.

574
00:34:51,531 --> 00:34:53,660
He's the talk of the town in this industry.

575
00:34:53,661 --> 00:34:58,931
- Yes. - But will Ji An go for it?

576
00:35:01,001 --> 00:35:02,971
The catharsis from imaginary revenge...

577
00:35:03,041 --> 00:35:05,241
can sometimes be a form of self-healing.

578
00:35:08,411 --> 00:35:11,151
Looks like my counseling has been quite helpful.

579
00:35:11,951 --> 00:35:14,221
Your depression, anxiety, and suicidal ideation scores...

580
00:35:14,281 --> 00:35:15,421
are much lower than before.

581
00:35:16,221 --> 00:35:18,421
Your social worker told me you found a job.

582
00:35:19,021 --> 00:35:20,521
Just cleaning buildings.

583
00:35:21,691 --> 00:35:25,231
Congratulations. You don't have to come in for sessions as often.

584
00:35:26,331 --> 00:35:30,431
I think once a month should be enough.

585
00:35:31,571 --> 00:35:32,571
Okay.

586
00:35:33,871 --> 00:35:34,901
Then we're all set.

587
00:35:37,741 --> 00:35:38,971
But, Doctor.

588
00:35:40,571 --> 00:35:44,511
I shouldn't actually turn that fantasy into reality, right?

589
00:35:48,681 --> 00:35:49,781
Young Ji.

590
00:35:50,451 --> 00:35:53,821
Imaginary revenge is just a counseling technique...

591
00:35:53,891 --> 00:35:54,921
I know.

592
00:35:56,661 --> 00:35:58,831
I was just saying.

593
00:36:00,361 --> 00:36:02,361
Right.

594
00:36:04,871 --> 00:36:05,871
Then we're all set.

595
00:36:11,871 --> 00:36:13,271
Oh, not again.

596
00:36:14,111 --> 00:36:15,241
Mr. Lee.

597
00:36:16,441 --> 00:36:17,481
Mr. Lee?

598
00:36:23,081 --> 00:36:24,181
Just a second.

599
00:36:26,351 --> 00:36:27,491
Yes, this is Cha Eun Hwan.

600
00:36:29,091 --> 00:36:30,121
Yes, where are...

601
00:36:34,861 --> 00:36:37,061
You're booking a session for who?

602
00:36:37,901 --> 00:36:40,430
Honestly, about the incident five years ago...

603
00:36:40,431 --> 00:36:42,601
He wasn't the only one doing wrong.

604
00:36:45,241 --> 00:36:46,641
No, that's not it.

605
00:36:47,271 --> 00:36:49,011
Honestly, the fact that you're still...

606
00:36:49,081 --> 00:36:52,451
so shaken up because of him... It's frustrating.

607
00:36:53,151 --> 00:36:56,451
In Kyung, desperately and sorrowfully, like you're wailing.

608
00:36:57,891 --> 00:36:59,551
(Director Kim Jin Uk)

609
00:36:59,951 --> 00:37:00,961
You...

610
00:37:01,791 --> 00:37:04,891
I... I love you so much.

611
00:37:07,091 --> 00:37:08,261
(Actor Jeong Da Eun)

612
00:37:19,641 --> 00:37:20,641
I...

613
00:37:20,811 --> 00:37:22,581
(Director Kim Jin Uk)

614
00:37:22,641 --> 00:37:25,511
- I love you. How could you... - Ji An.

615
00:37:26,281 --> 00:37:28,521
The mood is a little flat.

616
00:37:28,881 --> 00:37:30,851
Can we try it with a little more emotion?

617
00:37:31,521 --> 00:37:34,191
Let's go again. Cue.

618
00:37:36,391 --> 00:37:37,731
(Director Kim Jin Uk)

619
00:37:42,561 --> 00:37:43,561
Director.

620
00:37:44,801 --> 00:37:48,201
Let's take a quick break. I'm not feeling my best right now...

621
00:37:50,571 --> 00:37:53,541
(Director Kim Jin Uk)

622
00:37:53,611 --> 00:37:57,481
- Let's take a ten-minute break. - Okay.

623
00:38:07,151 --> 00:38:09,191
What? Therapy?

624
00:38:09,891 --> 00:38:12,591
What, do you think I'm some kind of psychopath?

625
00:38:12,791 --> 00:38:16,831
Hey, Yu Star, calm down. Hey.

626
00:38:17,131 --> 00:38:21,871
You're Gen Z. How can you have such an old-fashioned view of therapy?

627
00:38:22,301 --> 00:38:25,141
Even normal people go to therapy these days.

628
00:38:25,611 --> 00:38:26,811
Whatever. I don't want to.

629
00:38:27,571 --> 00:38:31,051
Hey, I'm telling you, it's not just any therapy, you know?

630
00:38:31,381 --> 00:38:34,751
It's apparently amazing at bringing out emotions...

631
00:38:35,021 --> 00:38:36,681
that people have suppressed in their subconscious.

632
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:39,321
Actors who have had sessions with him say...

633
00:38:39,391 --> 00:38:41,361
their acting improved dramatically.

634
00:38:46,091 --> 00:38:48,901
- I still don't want to. - Why?

635
00:38:48,961 --> 00:38:50,561
(J.An Entertainment)

636
00:38:51,331 --> 00:38:53,071
My private life is already public.

637
00:38:53,131 --> 00:38:55,171
Do I have to expose my subconscious too?

638
00:38:55,501 --> 00:38:57,741
What if the therapist starts spreading rumors about me?

639
00:38:57,811 --> 00:39:00,641
There's such a thing as professional ethics. You think he'd do that?

640
00:39:00,711 --> 00:39:02,081
If he did, there'd be rumors everywhere by now.

641
00:39:03,181 --> 00:39:04,211
Listen.

642
00:39:05,181 --> 00:39:07,181
You should not trust people.

643
00:39:07,681 --> 00:39:08,781
You're so naive.

644
00:39:09,351 --> 00:39:12,791
Forget it. I said no, so I'm leaving.

645
00:39:14,291 --> 00:39:15,361
Where do you think you're going?

646
00:39:15,891 --> 00:39:17,361
Hey, I heard Yi Jin went there.

647
00:39:23,701 --> 00:39:27,031
- What? - Her acting has gotten much better.

648
00:39:27,331 --> 00:39:29,171
It all adds up.

649
00:39:31,411 --> 00:39:33,671
(J.An Entertainment)

650
00:39:36,411 --> 00:39:39,051
You're sure this will be kept confidential?

651
00:39:44,051 --> 00:39:45,291
Yes, this is Cha Eun Hwan.

652
00:39:45,751 --> 00:39:48,021
You're booking a session for who?

653
00:39:48,791 --> 00:39:52,891
You know the actress, Yu Ji An? I'd like to book a session for her.

654
00:39:53,491 --> 00:39:55,531
Of course, I can assume it's completely confidential?

655
00:39:55,801 --> 00:39:57,601
(Counselor Cha Eun Hwan)

656
00:39:57,661 --> 00:39:59,371
Right. It's just a job.

657
00:39:59,871 --> 00:40:01,241
I'll just focus on that.

658
00:40:07,371 --> 00:40:08,511
Yes, come in.

659
00:40:10,781 --> 00:40:12,581
Can I really go home for the day?

660
00:40:13,381 --> 00:40:15,081
Yes, you can head out.

661
00:40:16,281 --> 00:40:18,421
Just who is this VIP client...

662
00:40:18,691 --> 00:40:20,491
that you're sending me home early? I'm a little offended.

663
00:40:20,551 --> 00:40:22,691
Come on, you know our center's claim to fame.

664
00:40:23,021 --> 00:40:24,061
Absolute...

665
00:40:24,731 --> 00:40:25,761
privacy.

666
00:40:26,931 --> 00:40:28,861
Well, getting to leave early is nice, but...

667
00:40:30,561 --> 00:40:31,601
Be careful with this.

668
00:40:31,971 --> 00:40:33,531
Don't forget and get locked in again...

669
00:40:33,601 --> 00:40:35,041
then don't call me crying like last time.

670
00:40:35,771 --> 00:40:36,971
Yes, I'll keep that in mind.

671
00:40:37,441 --> 00:40:39,311
- Go on. - Okay.

672
00:40:47,751 --> 00:40:49,921
What's with this rundown building?

673
00:40:50,521 --> 00:40:52,321
It looks more like a fortune teller's place.

674
00:40:52,551 --> 00:40:55,491
They said it's a therapy center. Let's give it a chance.

675
00:40:56,491 --> 00:40:59,131
Fine. Let's give it a chance.

676
00:41:03,161 --> 00:41:04,731
What? Are you coming with me?

677
00:41:05,001 --> 00:41:06,001
Are you going to go in alone?

678
00:41:07,101 --> 00:41:09,271
If every Tom, Dick, and Harry knows about it, how is that private?

679
00:41:09,801 --> 00:41:10,801
Stay here.

680
00:41:16,981 --> 00:41:17,981
Tom, Dick, and Harry?

681
00:41:18,151 --> 00:41:19,781
(Tok Tok Mental Care)

682
00:41:21,381 --> 00:41:23,051
(Notice: Building Power Outage, December 18)

683
00:41:23,121 --> 00:41:24,621
(Due to electrical work in the building,)

684
00:41:24,691 --> 00:41:26,421
(temporary power failures may occur.)

685
00:41:53,611 --> 00:41:56,151
Done looking at my face? Should we go in now?

686
00:42:00,151 --> 00:42:01,151
Please, come in.

687
00:42:18,211 --> 00:42:20,111
(New Client Intake Form)

688
00:42:20,171 --> 00:42:21,171
(Average)

689
00:42:24,341 --> 00:42:26,451
(Degrees, Certifications, Awards)

690
00:42:26,551 --> 00:42:27,921
I thought it was an exaggeration,

691
00:42:27,981 --> 00:42:30,181
but I guess the rumors about you being good are true.

692
00:42:30,651 --> 00:42:31,921
Well...

693
00:42:32,121 --> 00:42:35,221
I wouldn't know, but that's what I hear.

694
00:42:36,761 --> 00:42:37,961
That I'm quite skilled.

695
00:42:39,631 --> 00:42:43,301
So this is what it feels like. When people call me arrogant.

696
00:42:45,301 --> 00:42:47,371
Come over here and pick a card.

697
00:42:58,081 --> 00:42:59,711
You're very defensive.

698
00:43:01,051 --> 00:43:02,051
Am I?

699
00:43:02,881 --> 00:43:04,691
Your intake form is almost entirely gray.

700
00:43:05,191 --> 00:43:07,551
Always in the middle, between "no" and "yes."

701
00:43:08,021 --> 00:43:09,361
Neither black nor white.

702
00:43:10,191 --> 00:43:11,561
Only noncommittal choices.

703
00:43:11,791 --> 00:43:15,461
I don't know. I don't think of myself as defensive.

704
00:43:17,231 --> 00:43:19,771
Just now, you picked the first card without a second thought.

705
00:43:20,201 --> 00:43:23,071
Making an immediate choice to maintain a sense of control...

706
00:43:23,241 --> 00:43:25,241
is a classic trait of someone with strong defense mechanisms.

707
00:43:25,871 --> 00:43:27,311
During the selection process,

708
00:43:27,641 --> 00:43:29,611
they're afraid of revealing their inner selves.

709
00:43:32,081 --> 00:43:33,451
What was your childhood like?

710
00:43:35,121 --> 00:43:36,281
Why do you want to know?

711
00:43:38,891 --> 00:43:40,691
This is your session, Yu Ji An.

712
00:43:41,761 --> 00:43:43,421
A person's disposition is mostly shaped...

713
00:43:43,821 --> 00:43:45,691
by their childhood experiences.

714
00:43:46,061 --> 00:43:47,761
Especially their relationship with their parents.

715
00:43:49,261 --> 00:43:50,361
How was yours?

716
00:43:51,531 --> 00:43:52,531
Was it a good one?

717
00:43:54,971 --> 00:43:56,041
Well...

718
00:43:57,641 --> 00:43:58,641
Not particularly...

719
00:43:59,211 --> 00:44:00,241
good...

720
00:44:01,381 --> 00:44:02,641
or bad.

721
00:44:03,741 --> 00:44:04,851
It was average.

722
00:44:05,351 --> 00:44:06,411
Yu Ji An.

723
00:44:07,051 --> 00:44:08,951
The client needs to be honest...

724
00:44:09,451 --> 00:44:11,321
for us to have an effective session.

725
00:44:18,891 --> 00:44:23,031
You feel intense fear when you're alone on a rainy day.

726
00:44:24,661 --> 00:44:26,571
It's also accompanied by claustrophobia...

727
00:44:26,631 --> 00:44:28,301
which you don't normally experience.

728
00:44:32,611 --> 00:44:34,171
Just like the weather today.

729
00:44:36,311 --> 00:44:38,111
It's not that serious.

730
00:44:38,581 --> 00:44:40,681
A fear that responds to a specific condition...

731
00:44:40,981 --> 00:44:44,051
is a conditioned trigger response. A form of trauma.

732
00:44:45,391 --> 00:44:46,491
In your childhood,

733
00:44:47,451 --> 00:44:50,291
did you ever experience a major accident?

734
00:44:59,531 --> 00:45:00,531
Excuse me a moment.

735
00:45:30,261 --> 00:45:32,571
Yes, we're closed for the day.

736
00:45:34,571 --> 00:45:36,471
What? A power failure?

737
00:45:36,971 --> 00:45:40,911
Open the door. I said, open the door. Please, just open the door.

738
00:45:43,111 --> 00:45:44,211
Claustrophobia.

739
00:45:46,611 --> 00:45:48,581
Open the door.

740
00:45:48,651 --> 00:45:51,421
Ji An. Ji An, are you okay? Can you hear me?

741
00:45:52,291 --> 00:45:56,561
- Ji An. - Please open the door. Open it.

742
00:45:57,491 --> 00:45:59,461
Please, open the door.

743
00:46:01,601 --> 00:46:03,001
(Tok Tok Mental Care)

744
00:46:03,061 --> 00:46:04,661
Please, open the door.

745
00:46:04,731 --> 00:46:06,831
Ji An, you need to step away from the door, okay?

746
00:46:07,971 --> 00:46:09,171
Open the door...

747
00:46:10,501 --> 00:46:13,271
Please... Please help me.

748
00:46:20,081 --> 00:46:22,481
(Tok Tok Mental Care)

749
00:46:24,121 --> 00:46:26,421
Please, open the door.

750
00:46:29,421 --> 00:46:31,391
(Tok Tok Mental Care)

751
00:46:35,831 --> 00:46:36,961
Ji An, are you okay?

752
00:46:37,701 --> 00:46:40,201
I can't breathe.

753
00:46:42,171 --> 00:46:43,641
Look at me. Look into my eyes.

754
00:46:45,671 --> 00:46:48,441
Okay, now just do what I do. All right?

755
00:46:49,781 --> 00:46:51,651
Breathe in. One, two.

756
00:46:52,911 --> 00:46:54,551
Breathe out. Three, four.

757
00:46:58,551 --> 00:47:00,791
Good. You're doing great. One more time.

758
00:47:32,221 --> 00:47:35,291
Hey, kid, snap out of it. Hey, kid.

759
00:47:35,991 --> 00:47:38,361
I promise I'll save you.

760
00:47:46,171 --> 00:47:47,171
I'm sorry.

761
00:47:48,371 --> 00:47:49,371
Mister.

762
00:47:52,471 --> 00:47:53,511
Sorry...

